ttention_weights":[],"max_activation":6.972200393676758,"max_token_index":652,"peak_labels":{"hate speech":"none","language":"en","names":"none","part of speech":"NOUN","personal data":"none","postal addresses":"none","source":"ultrachat","toxicity":"none"},"text":"<|im_start|>system\nYou are a helpful assistant.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nCan you share any favorite snacks that are high in protein and low in sugar to help curb cravings during times of stress or anxiety?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nHere are some favorite high-protein, low-sugar snacks:\n\n1. Greek yogurt with berries\n2. Hard-boiled eggs\n3. Edamame\n4. Roasted chickpeas\n5. Cottage cheese with cucumber slices\n6. Hummus with carrot sticks or cucumber slices\n7. Turkey or beef jerky\n8. Almonds, walnuts, or pistachios\n9. Protein bars (look for ones with low sugar and high protein)\n10. Protein shakes or smoothies (made with unsweetened almond milk, protein powder, and frozen berries for sweetness)<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nOh wow, those are really good suggestions! I never thought about roasted chickpeas as a snack option. Do you have any recipes or seasonings you recommend for them?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nYes! Roasted chickpeas are a great high-protein snack option. Here's a recipe for roasted chickpeas:\n\nIngredients:\n- 1 can of chickpeas, drained and rinsed\n- 1 tablespoon olive oil\n- Salt & pepper\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n\nInstructions:\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F.\n2. Spread the chickpeas on a clean kitchen towel and pat them dry.\n3. In a small bowl, mix together olive oil, salt, pepper, chili powder, cumin, and garlic powder.\n4. Add the chickpeas to the bowl and coat them well with the spice mixture.\n5. Spread the chickpeas evenly on a baking sheet and bake for 25-30 minutes or until crispy.\n6. Allow the chickpeas to cool before serving.\n\nYou can also try other seasoning combinations such as paprika and cayenne pepper, cinnamon and sugar, or rosemary and garlic.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nWow, that recipe sounds amazing! I can't wait to try it out. Do you have any other recipes for high-protein snacks that are easy to make at home?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nYes, here are a few more easy high-protein snack recipes:\n\n1. Peanut Butter Banana Yogurt:\n- 1 cup Greek yogurt\n- 1 tablespoon peanut butter\n- 1 banana, sliced\n- drizzle of honey (optional)\n\nInstructions: \nIn a small bowl, mix together the Greek yogurt and peanut butter. Top with sliced banana and a drizzle of honey for a sweet treat that's high in protein.\n\n2. Turkey and Cheese Roll-ups:\n- Sliced turkey breast\n- Sliced cheese (cheddar or Swiss work well)\n- Toothpicks\n\nInstructions: \nLay a slice of turkey breast on a cutting board. Top with a slice of cheese and roll up tightly. Cut into bite-sized pieces and secure with a toothpick.\n\n3. Protein-Packed Trail Mix: \n- Almonds\n- Pistachios\n- Pumpkin seeds\n- Sunflower seeds \n- Dried cranberries or raisins \n- Dark chocolate chips (optional)\n\nInstructions: \nCombine all ingredients in a bowl and mix well. Store in an airtight container for a grab-and-go snack that's high in protein and energy-boosting nutrients. \n\nI hope these recipes are helpful! Enjoy!<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nDo","tokens":["<|im_start|>","system","\n","You"," are"," a"," helpful"," assistant",".","<|im_end|>","\n","<|im_start|>","user","\n","Can"," you"," share"," any"," favorite"," snacks"," that"," are"," high"," in"," protein"," and"," low"," in"," sugar"," to"," help"," curb"," cravings"," during"," times"," of"," stress"," or"," anxiety","?","<|im_end|>","\n","<|im_start|>","assistant","\n","Here"," are"," some"," favorite"," high","-pro","tein",","," low","-s","ugar"," snacks",":\n\n","1","."," Greek"," yogurt"," with"," berries","\n","2","."," Hard","-bo","iled"," eggs","\n","3","."," Ed","am","ame","\n","4","."," Ro","asted"," chick","pe","as","\n","5